":["Q9UGI0"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables K63-linked polyubiquitin modification-dependent protein binding activity and thiol-dependent deubiquitinase. Involved in several processes, including positive regulation of Wnt signaling pathway; protein deubiquitination; and regulation of cell morphogenesis. Located in cytosol and nucleoplasm. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9UGI0","text":"Ubiquitin thioesterase, which specifically hydrolyzes 'Lys-29'-linked and 'Lys-33'-linked diubiquitin (PubMed:22157957, PubMed:23827681, PubMed:25752573, PubMed:25752577). Also cleaves 'Lys-63'-linked chains, but with 40-fold less efficiency compared to 'Lys-29'-linked ones (PubMed:18281465). Positive regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway that deubiquitinates APC protein, a negative regulator of Wnt-mediated transcription (PubMed:18281465). Acts as a regulator of autophagy by mediating deubiquitination of PIK3C3/VPS34, thereby promoting autophagosome maturation (PubMed:33637724). Plays a role in the regulation of cell morphology and cytoskeletal organization (PubMed:21834987). Required in the stress fiber dynamics and cell migration (PubMed:21834987)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}